<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-UHISPANK TAKES TWO NEW BOARD MEMBERS.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-UHISPANK TAKES TWO NEW BOARD MEMBERS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uhispank said on Monday that its board has decided to take two new board members.</p>
<p>The new members are Lembit Kitter and Urmas Putsepp, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Kitter has been Uhispank's general manager from May 21, and Putsepp was appointed the bank's finance director from the same date.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
